course: dictionary
lesson: 7186
title: Perspire: the polite word for sweat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Perspire means to sweat. Your body gives off a little liquid through your skin when you are hot, nervous or working hard. Sweat is the everyday word. Perspire is the polite or formal word, the kind you hear in adverts and from doctors.
explain: Context gives you the meaning. «Dig till you gently perspire» is from a garden poem, and the word gently is the clue: it means you sweat a little, not a lot. The poem tells you what the word does, so you can work it out.
explain: Science lessons use perspire to explain how the body cools down. Sweat dries on the skin and takes heat away, so you feel cooler. To check a meaning, swap the word into a sentence: «I begin to sweat» and «I begin to perspire» mean the same thing.
fact: Perspire means to sweat, to give off liquid through your skin.
fact: You perspire when you are hot, nervous or working hard.
fact: Perspire is the polite or formal word; sweat is the everyday word.
fact: Phrases you may see: perspire heavily, begin to perspire.
fact: Sweat dries on your skin and takes heat away, which helps your body cool down.
exercise: «Dig till you gently perspire.» What does perspire mean in this poem? | *To sweat a little | To stop working | To cry loudly | To sleep under a tree
exercise: Which word is the everyday word for perspire? | *Sweat | Freeze | Sing | Yawn
exercise: Why might a doctor say «you may perspire heavily» instead of «you may sweat a lot»? | Perspire is simply a longer word | Perspire means to be cold | Perspire means to sleep | *Perspire is the polite, formal word
test: Which sentence uses perspire correctly? | The soup began to perspire | Her pencil began to perspire | The clock began to perspire | *After the hill climb, Sam began to perspire heavily
test: Your body cools down because sweat does what? | *Dries on your skin and takes heat away | Makes you sleepy | Turns into ice | Stays on your skin forever
exam: Mrs Patel says, «You may perspire when you are nervous.» What does perspire mean? | *To give off liquid through your skin | To sing | To sleep
